# What must never reach the image.
#
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so without this file everything in the
# working tree is baked into a layer — and a layer is not a secret. Anyone who
# can `docker pull`, `docker save` or read `docker history` gets whatever was
# copied, and deleting it in a later layer does not remove it from the earlier
# one.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------
# .env is gitignored, so it is absent from a clone and present on every machine
# that follows the setup instructions — which makes a local `docker compose
# build` the likely way GROQ_API_KEY and DATABASE_URL end up in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Host-specific and huge -------------------------------------------
# A virtualenv holds binaries built for the host, which are wrong for the image
# and hundreds of megabytes of wrong.
.venv/
venv/
ENV/

# Full history, including any secret ever committed and later removed.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Not needed at runtime --------------------------------------------
# Excluded so that editing a test or a document does not invalidate the image
# layer and force a rebuild of everything after it.
tests/
docs/
observability/results/
*.md
!README.md

.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# The stack's own configuration is bind-mounted by docker-compose at run time,
# never copied into the app image.
observability/prometheus/
observability/grafana/
observability/filebeat/
observability/kibana/
observability/elasticsearch/
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
